.TH ALL_PYTHON.PY 1 "2026-03-28" "1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
all_python.py \- discover and manage all Python installations on macOS or Windows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 all_python.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B all_python.py
scans the system for every Python installation — Homebrew, pyenv, conda, system,
and official installer — and presents them in a colour-coded table showing
version, architecture, pip availability, vendor, aliases, and path.
.PP
Running without flags launches an interactive loop. Flags like
.B \-\-list
and
.B \-\-switch
provide non-interactive, scriptable equivalents of every action.
.PP
All per-binary queries (version, architecture, pip, site-packages) run in
parallel via
.B ThreadPoolExecutor
so scans are fast even with many installations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print the installation table and exit without entering interactive mode.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output all installations as a JSON array and exit. Includes
.IR version ", " vendor ", " arch ", " pip ", " commands ", " path ", " site_packages ", " is_default ", " protected .
.TP
.BI \-\-switch " N"
Non-interactively switch the default Python to installation number
.IR N
(as shown in the
.B #
column). Prints the table first so the index is visible.
.TP
.BI \-\-remove " N"
Non-interactively remove installation number
.IR N .
Subject to the same safety guardrails as the interactive
.B R
action.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Add a
.B SITE-PACKAGES
column showing each installation's site-packages directory.
Also enables site-packages collection when used with
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color codes. Useful when piping output to other tools.
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " FIELD"
Sort installations by
.BR version " (default, descending),"
.BR vendor ", or"
.BR path .
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
When launched without
.BR \-\-list ", " \-\-json ", " \-\-switch ", or " \-\-remove ,
the tool enters an interactive loop. After displaying the table it presents:
.RS
.TP
.B S
Switch Default — prompts for an installation number, then writes
.B alias python=
and
.B alias python3=
entries to
.I ~/.zshrc
(or
.I ~/.bash_profile
on bash). Backs up the file before writing. On Windows, updates the PowerShell profile.
.TP
.B R
Remove Version — prompts for a number, runs safety checks, then removes the
selected installation. See
.B SAFETY GUARDRAILS
below.
.TP
.B E " / Enter"
Exit.
.RE
.SH TABLE COLUMNS
.TP
.B #
Selection index for
.B \-\-switch
and
.B \-\-remove .
.TP
.B VERSION
Full
.I x.y.z
version. Green for 3.x, red for 2.x, yellow otherwise.
.TP
.B ARCH
.BR "Apple Silicon" ", " "Intel 64" ", " Universal " (macOS);"
.BR "64-bit" " or " "32-bit" " (Windows)."
.TP
.B PIP
Whether
.B pip
is available for this installation.
.TP
.B VENDOR
Source of the installation. See
.BR "VENDOR DETECTION" .
.TP
.B ALIASES
Binary names that resolve to this installation
.RI ( python ", " python3 ", etc.)."
.TP
.B LOCATION
Resolved real path. Annotated with
.B (Current Default)
or
.B (Protected)
where applicable.
.TP
.B SITE-PACKAGES
.RI ( \-\-verbose " only)"
Path to the site-packages directory.
.SH VENDOR DETECTION
.TS
l l.
macOS System	Path under /usr/bin or /System/Library
Homebrew	Path contains homebrew or Cellar
Official Installer	Path under /Library/Frameworks/Python.framework
pyenv	Path contains .pyenv
Conda	Path contains anaconda or miniconda
Microsoft Store	Path contains WindowsApps (Windows; marked Protected)
User/Other	Everything else
.TE
.SH SAFETY GUARDRAILS
Removal is blocked with an error message if the target is:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
A Protected or System installation (macOS system Python, Microsoft Store)
.IP \(bu 2
The currently active default Python
.IP \(bu 2
The Python interpreter currently running the script
.RE
.PP
On Windows, all removal requests are redirected to
.B "Settings > Apps > Installed Apps"
to avoid corrupting the Windows Registry.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Interactive mode:
.EX
python3 all_python.py
.EE
.TP
List all installations non-interactively:
.EX
python3 all_python.py --list
.EE
.TP
List with site-packages paths:
.EX
python3 all_python.py --list --verbose
.EE
.TP
Output as JSON for scripting:
.EX
python3 all_python.py --json
.EE
.TP
Switch default to installation #3:
.EX
python3 all_python.py --switch 3
.EE
.TP
Remove installation #2:
.EX
python3 all_python.py --remove 2
.EE
.TP
Sort by vendor, no color, pipe to grep:
.EX
python3 all_python.py --list --sort vendor --no-color | grep Conda
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.zshrc " / " ~/.bash_profile
Modified by
.B Switch Default
on macOS. Backed up before writing as
.IR ~/.zshrc.backup-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS .
.TP
.I ~/Documents/WindowsPowerShell/Microsoft.PowerShell_profile.ps1
Modified by
.B Switch Default
on Windows. Backed up before writing.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.10 or later, macOS or Windows.
.PP
.B lipo
is required for architecture detection on macOS (included with Xcode Command Line Tools).
.PP
.B brew
is required to uninstall Homebrew-managed installations (optional — manual path is printed otherwise).
.SH AUTHOR
Anirban Bagchi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python3 (1),
.BR brew (1),
.BR pyenv (1)
